    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `getLocality()` sits naturally in this codebase:\n\n- **Right unit.** `locality` is derived purely from the owner's own `city` field, so deriving it on `Owner` is the correct home. This also matches an existing precedent in the same class \u2014 the `SILVER`/`BRONZE` derived method is already a computed string getter on `Owner`, so `getLocality()` follows the established local convention rather than introducing a new pattern.\n- **No duplication / no catch-all drift.** The lookup table is a single private `static final` constant, and the getter is a one-line `getOrDefault`. Nothing is copied, and the method is a thin, cohesive addition rather than bloating the class with unrelated responsibility.\n- **Idiomatic.** `Map.of(...)` + `getOrDefault(city, \"UNKNOWN\")` is the conventional Java expression of a fixed lookup-with-default, and the empty-city case falls through to `\"UNKNOWN\"` via the same path.\n- **Consistent surface.** The OpenAPI `locality` schema is placed alongside the sibling derived/`readOnly` properties (next to the tier and `householdId` fields), with a description matching the model's Javadoc \u2014 the API contract stays coherent with the model.",
